\
## **Grounding & Embodiment Basics**\
\
1. **Orienting** \'96 Slowly look around your space, letting your gaze land on neutral or pleasant objects. Name them silently: "lamp," "tree," "blue cup." \
\
2. **5-4-3-2-1 Sensing** \'96 Name 5 things you see, 4 you hear, 3 you can touch, 2 you smell, 1 you taste. \
\
3. **Foot Grounding** \'96 Stand with feet hip-width apart. Shift weight forward/back, side to side. Visualize roots growing from your feet into the earth. \
\
4. **Body Scan for Contact Points** \'96 Feel where your body meets the chair/floor. Notice the weight of your body being held by the surface beneath you. \
\
5. **Hand on Heart, Hand on Belly** \'96 Self-hold while breathing slowly. Feel the warmth and containment of your own touch. \
\
6. **Closed Loop Connection** \'96 Cross arms, tuck hands under opposite armpits, cross ankles, tuck chin. Hold 30-60 seconds to feel contained. \
\
7. **Self-Holding (Forehead + Heart)** \'96 One palm on forehead, one on heart. Alternate attention between the hands, then feel from inside the body what each hand senses. \
\
8. **Grounded Walking** \'96 Walk slowly, feeling each foot contact the ground. Notice the roll from heel to toe. \
\
---\
\
## **Breathwork & Vocal Toning**\
\
9. **Equal Breathing (4-4)** \'96 Inhale 4 counts, exhale 4 counts through the nose. Repeat 5-10 times. \
\
10. **Pursed Lip Breathing** \'96 Inhale through nose, exhale through pursed lips (like blowing out a candle). Make exhales longer than inhales. \
\
11. **Voo Sound (Vagal Toning)** \'96 Inhale deeply, exhale with a low "vooooo" sound, feeling vibrations in chest. Repeat 3-5 times. \
\
12. **Humming** \'96 Inhale, then hum on the exhale. Notice vibrations in chest, throat, face. Adjust pitch to find what soothes. \
\
13. **Back-to-Front Breathing** \'96 As you exhale, play with sounds: "ahhhh," "psssss," "hmm." Feel the vibration. Empty until the sound is gone. \
\
14. **Rib Breathing** \'96 Place hands on sides of ribs. Gently squeeze on exhale, release on inhale. Then try on head. \
\
15. **Diaphragmatic Breathing** \'96 Lie down, hand on chest, hand on belly. Breathe so only the belly hand moves. \
\
---\
\
## **Self-Soothing Touch**\
\
16. **Butterfly Hug** \'96 Cross arms over chest, hands on collarbones. Alternate tapping left-right-left-right slowly while breathing. \
\
17. **Arm Squeeze** \'96 Squeeze opposite arms, experimenting with pressure and speed. Feel the contrast between squeezed and released. \
\
18. **Palm Glide** \'96 Place palms on tops of thighs near hips. Press in, then glide down toward knees on exhale. \
\
19. **Self-Hug with Sway** \'96 Wrap arms around yourself, gently sway side to side. \
\
20. **Soft Brushing** \'96 Lightly brush your own arms, legs, or face with fingertips. \
\
21. **Full Body Squeeze** \'96 Tense entire body on inhale, release completely on exhale. \
\
---\
\
## **Movement & Shaking**\
\
22. **Shake It Out** \'96 Stand or sit with feet grounded. Let hands, arms, legs tremble naturally without forcing. Rest and notice after. \
\
23. **Tremoring** \'96 Allow gentle shaking to travel from hands up through shoulders, into torso, down through legs. Let it be involuntary. \
\
24. **Cat-Cow Flow** \'96 On all fours, inhale arch back (cow), exhale round spine (cat). Connect breath to movement. \
\
25. **Child's Pose** \'96 Kneel, toes together, knees apart, fold forward resting torso between thighs. Arms extended or by sides. \
\
26. **Legs Up the Wall** \'96 Lie with hips against wall, legs extended up. Rest arms comfortably. Stay 5-20 minutes. \
\
27. **Knees to Chest** \'96 Lie on back, pull knees toward chest, then gently toward shoulders. Hold 30 seconds. \
\
28. **Reach for the Stars** \'96 Stand, reach both arms up as if grabbing stars from the night sky. Keep reaching until arms tire, then release slowly. \
\
29. **Hedgehog Curl** \'96 Curl into a tight ball starting from chest inward. Notice breath. Feel if it's safe or unsafe. Slowly unfurl. \
\
30. **Seated Pelvic Shift** \'96 Sit and gently rock pelvis forward and back, finding stability through movement. \
\
31. **Freeing the Spine** \'96 Gentle rotations, side bends, and movements to mobilize back, ribs, neck, shoulders. \
\
32. **Trigger Point Release** \'96 Use a tennis ball or foam roller against wall/floor to release shoulder/neck tension. \
\
---\
\
## **Somatic Awareness & Tracking**\
\
33. **Tracking Sensations** \'96 Scan body for one area of tension and one neutral area. Slowly pendulate attention between them. \
\
34. **Hand Space Awareness** \'96 Close fist tightly. Open slowly, noticing the space between each finger. Close again. Observe the space. \
\
35. **Body Mapping** \'96 Draw an outline of your body and mark where you feel sensations, tension, or emotions. \
\
36. **Interoceptive Check-In** \'96 Close eyes. Notice heartbeat, temperature, muscle tension, digestive feelings, breath rhythm. \
\
37. **Cupping the Eyes** \'96 Sit comfortably, elbows on knees, cup palms over eyes (not pressing). Breathe in the darkness for 3 breaths. \
\
38. **Soft Eyes** \'96 Focus on one object, then soften gaze until it blurs. Close eyes, wait for body to relax, reopen. \
\
---\
\
## **Playful & Expressive**\
\
39. **Finding Your Groove** \'96 Put on music and let your body find its natural rhythm. Dance without choreography. \
\
40. **Mood State Movement** \'96 Notice how you're feeling, then move your body *as if* you felt the opposite. Exaggerate the shift. \
\
41. **Primal Sounds** \'96 Let yourself sigh, groan, hum, or make whatever sound your body wants to release. \
\
42. **Collecting Stars** (variation) \'96 Reach up and "grab" imaginary stars, bringing them down to different parts of your body. \
\
43. **Animal Movements** \'96 Crawl like a bear, shake like a dog, stretch like a cat, roll like an otter. \
\
---\
\
## **Resourcing & Imagery**\
\
44. **Recalling a Kindness** \'96 Remember a time someone was kind to you. Notice how your body recalls it\'97sensations, warmth, expansion. \
\
45. **Safe Place Visualization** \'96 Imagine a place where you feel completely safe. Feel it in your body\'97temperature, posture, breath. \
\
46. **Root Visualization** \'96 Imagine roots extending from your spine or feet deep into the earth, drawing up stability. \
\
47. **Ideokinesis (Imagined Movement)** \'96 Visualize releasing weight or tension without actually moving. Let the image facilitate the shift. \
\
---\
\
## **Water & Nature Based**\
\
48. **Cold Water on Wrists** \'96 Run cool water over your wrists or hold a cold water bottle. Notice temperature change. \
\
49. **Barefoot Grounding** \'96 Stand barefoot on grass, dirt, or concrete. Feel the texture, temperature, connection to earth. \
\
50. **Water Drinking Meditation** \'96 Sip room temperature water or warm tea slowly. Notice scent, taste, warmth, movement down throat. \
\
51. **Ice Cube Hold** \'96 Hold an ice cube briefly. Intense sensation brings you immediately to present moment. \
\
---\
\
## **Quick Regulation Hacks**\
\
52. **Progressive Muscle Relaxation** \'96 Tense feet on inhale, release on exhale. Move up through legs, belly, chest, arms, face. \
\
53. **Titration** \'96 When overwhelmed, touch into a sensation for just 2-3 seconds, then resource (butterfly hug, safe memory). Repeat. \
\
54. **Boundary Practice** \'96 Extend arms to sides, push against a wall or doorframe. Feel your edges, your "no," your container. \
\
55. **Centering** \'96 Hand on heart, hand on belly, back against wall. Feel spine supported, core aligned. \
\
---\
\
**Pick one that calls to you right now.** The body doesn't need perfection\'97just attention.\
\
\
